/* ============================================================================
paired-t-test.epher -- systolic pressure before and after a program

Tests whether an eight-week program changed systolic blood pressure,
using the builtin paired t test ttestpaired(before, after) (guide
1.20): one person, two measurements, so the test works on the seven
before-minus-after differences. It prints the t statistic and the
two-sided p-value as a display string. The lines above show the
differences and their mean and standard deviation.

Run it from a terminal:
  Linux (deb, rpm):  epher /usr/lib/epher/scripts/statistics/tests/paired-t-test.epher
  Windows:           epher "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\epher\scripts\statistics\tests\paired-t-test.epher"
  macOS:             epher /Applications/epher.app/Contents/Resources/scripts/statistics/tests/paired-t-test.epher
In the REPL:             load one of the paths above
Web/desktop:             paste the whole file into the entry, press Enter
Everything also works line by line in the TUI.

The knobs to edit are `before` and `after` below. Everything above the
results section is machinery you can leave alone.
============================================================================ */

// ---- the knobs -----------------------------------------------------------------
const before = {147, 140, 154, 140, 147, 147, 140}   // systolic, mm Hg, before
const after = {142, 139, 150, 140, 144, 145, 141}    // systolic, mm Hg, after

// ---- helpers: the differences and their spread ------------------------------------
def sdd() = sqrt(variance(before - after) * len(before - after) / (len(before - after) - 1)) // sample stdev of the differences

// ---- what the test sees --------------------------------------------------------------
print("differences, before minus after:", before - after)
print("mean difference:", mean(before - after))
print("sample stdev of the differences:", sdd())

// ---- the test ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ttestpaired(before, after)  // t = 2.4495, p = 0.0498: the drop is just
                            // significant at the 5% level, so the program
                            // measurably lowered systolic pressure here

/* ---- expected output ----
= {147, 140, 154, 140, 147, 147, 140}
= {142, 139, 150, 140, 144, 145, 141}
= differences, before minus after: {5, 1, 4, 0, 3, 2, -1}
= mean difference: 2
= sample stdev of the differences: 2.16024689947
= t = 2.4495, p = 0.0498
*/